# GitHub App credentials, mounted only into github-token. Optional: a level without credentials
# can't issue tokens; nothing else is affected.
#
# Variables are prefixed with the upper-cased level name from github-token/levels.json. Give each
# level its own App with only these permissions and no webhook (Metadata is added automatically):
#   github_read: read-only Actions, Artifact metadata, Checks, Code quality, Commit statuses,
#                Contents, Deployments, Pull requests
#   github_pr:   read and write Contents and Pull requests. Never Workflows. Only the org rulesets
#                in README.md limit pushes to apollo/* branches; create them before installing.
#
# Installation ID: the end of https://github.com/organizations/<org>/settings/installations/<id>
# Private keys go on one line: base64 < your-app.private-key.pem | tr -d '\n'
GITHUB_READ_APP_ID=
GITHUB_READ_INSTALLATION_ID=
GITHUB_READ_PRIVATE_KEY_BASE64=
GITHUB_PR_APP_ID=
GITHUB_PR_INSTALLATION_ID=
GITHUB_PR_PRIVATE_KEY_BASE64=
